# Python bytecode from running the skill's scripts.
#
# `quick_validate.py` and `init_skill.py` are executed by the skill's own
# walkthrough and by `do-harness eval`, so CPython writes a `__pycache__`
# directory here next to the sources. Those artifacts are interpreter- and
# version-specific (e.g. `quick_validate.cpython-313.pyc`), must never be
# committed, and are regenerated on demand — so the whole cache is ignored.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
